WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:08.740
When Senator Elizabeth Warren delivered a speech at a campaign event in Atlanta last November,

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.580
charter school supports showed up
to make their voices heard.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:17.820
Sarah Carpenter, a grandmother and school choice activist, who had traveled six hours from Memphis

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.620
to attend the event, confronted Warren backstage.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.119
That clip went viral because Warren wasn't
telling the truth.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.000
Three weeks earlier an education researcher named Corey DeAngelis

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:41.220
had discovered through online sleuthing that her son Alex Warren, now 43, had attended Kirby Hall,

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.620
an elite private school in Austin.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.480
DeAngelis, who is the director of school choice at the Reason Foundation,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.360
the nonprofit that publishes Reason TV,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.080
decided to research the issue because Warren wasn't forthcoming with reporters.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.800
A few journalists actually asked all the democratic presidential candidates

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.420
where they sent their own kids to school, and where they went to school, just as some descriptive

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.260
analysis and reporting, which is very interesting.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.340
And going through that I saw that Elizabeth
Warren did respond to their email and said that

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.780
she went to public schools in Oklahoma,
but the campaign said no response on the question of

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.960
where she sent her own kids to school.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.020
So I started thinking a little bit, you know,
if she's so public school proud,

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.800
and that she's bragging about how she went to public schools, and how she taught at public school,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.860
she'd probably be really proud to talk about how she sent her own kids to public schools

00:01:30.860 --> 00:03:13.000
if that was actually the case.

